00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Cytokinetics, Incorporated is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.8B market cap on $88M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -166% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $535M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -13.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 128% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (19.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 695% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their persona